{"labs": [{"stimuli": [{"id": 0, "type": "welcome", "contents": [{}], "template_override": 1, "_data": []}, {"id": 1, "contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "enpe7n5le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n5le01ob11re2aud01", "images": [{"id": 0, "image": "enpe7n5le01ob11re2img01.jpg", "text": "<strong>Sean</strong>: Hi, Kelly. Have you studied for the exam next week? I did a lot of research last night, but there are some things I haven't understood yet.\n<br/><strong>Kelly</strong>: Sure, I studied. I also read many articles and books about the topic, and I think I've done pretty well with it. Do you have any question I can help you with?\n<br/><strong>Sean</strong>: In fact, I have plenty of doubts, but I won't ask you a lot of questions. First, I don't understand the necessity of an accessible application and what it can do in the .NET framework.\n<br/><strong>Kelly</strong>: For example, my uncle hasn't managed his company for a long time now, but he has run the show enough time to know what a company needs in order to succeed. He said accessible applications had positive implications for his business. Now, in order to make it possible, five accessibility requirements need to be taken into account. According to those, an accessible application will hold up high contrast mode, arrange keyboard access to all features, and avoid transmitting relevant information by sound among others.", "time": ""}, {"id": 1, "image": "enpe7n5le01ob11re2img02.jpg", "text": "<strong>Sean</strong>: Alright. Have you ever done that in the .NET framework?\n<br/><strong>Kelly</strong>: Yes, I have done some projects. I helped my uncle with one three months ago. You can create the application by selecting a project type and a pattern; then, you have to determine a name in the 'new project' dialog box. You can add controls and organize properties in order to make an accessible application.", "time": "74000"}, {"id": 2, "image": "enpe7n5le01ob11re2img03.jpg", "text": "<s