but you can use unspecific expressions such as: never, ever, for, since, already, yet, etc.<br/><br/><strong>Negative and question</strong>:<br/><br/> The negative form of a present perfect sentence is made with the auxiliary in negative <strong>hasn't</strong> (he, she, it) or <strong>haven't</strong> (I, you, we, they) and the verb in past participle. <br/><br/>Questions are made by switching the position of the auxiliary and the subject. <br/><br/>Take a look at this structures:", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Subject</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Auxiliary</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Verb in past participle</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Complement</strong> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"haven't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"an application before.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Interrogative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Auxiliary</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Subject</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Verb in past participle</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Complement</strong> \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Have\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"you\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"done\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"an application before?\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}", "type": "table"}, {"content": "<strong>Past Simple</strong><br/><br/>As past simple is used when you talk about something that happen in a specific time before now, you can use past time expressions such as: yesterday, ago, last, etc. <br/><br/><strong>Negative and questions</strong><br/><br/>The negative form of a past simple sentence is made with the auxiliary <strong>did</strong> in negative <strong>didn't</strong> and the verb in base form.<br/>Questions are made by switching the position of the auxiliary and the subject.<br/><br/>Take a look at this structures:<br/> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":3,\"columns\":4,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Negative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Subject</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Auxiliary</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>Ver in base form</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<strong>complement</strong>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"I\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"didn't\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"do\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \